Keeps the LMS positions of libsais_main_8u's first pass over T for after
the recursion, where the free space allows, instead of finding them again.

After the recursion has sorted the reduced string, libsais_main_8u maps
its suffix array back to positions in T through the list of LMS
positions, which it rebuilds with a second classification pass over T
(libsais_gather_lms_suffixes_8u). Here the list from the first pass is
copied into the last m ints of the free space, and the top level and the
recursion work in the fs - m ints below it. That is done only where
fs >= m, which puts the copy beyond SA[0..n), and fs + n >= 4m, which
leaves the recursion fs + n - 3m >= m ints of free space, at least its
length: a level's free space less its length never decreases down the
recursion and a level's alphabet is smaller than its length, so the
recursion still never allocates. Elsewhere the positions are found again
as before. The suffix array is the same either way.

Only libsais_main_8u changes, and every entry that reaches it (libsais,
libsais_gsa, libsais_bwt, libsais_bwt_aux and their _ctx forms) takes the
same path. The recursion's levels still find their own positions again:
in most of its bucket layouts that pass also recounts the buckets, which
the deeper levels overwrite, so keeping the positions there saves less.

At level 9 the condition holds for every block of a 16 KiB stream and for
the 900 kB blocks of inputs with at most 3/8 LMS positions (XA:Z, quality
strings, ten of the twelve Silesia files), not for those of MC:Z (0.40).

Measured on the M4 with Apple clang 21, bz2-ng's encoder at level 9, 5
rounds interleaved with an identical-binary control, each speed taken
relative to stock libbz2's in the same process, against the same build
without this patch (both builds also carrying an unconditional read
prefetch in two partial-sorting and two final-sorting scans of the
recursion, a change that measured even there and is not in this series):
XA:Z whole 1.061, quality strings whole 1.057, Silesia 1.035, and in
16 KiB streams XA:Z 1.057 and MC:Z 1.041, faster in every round; quality
strings in 16 KiB streams 1.019, inside the noise of the raw speeds, and
MC:Z whole 0.987, inside the noise.

--- a/libsais.c
+++ b/libsais.c
@@ -1,3 +1,10 @@
+/*
+ * Altered for bz2-ng: this is libsais.c of libsais commit 1a696e6 with the
+ * following patches from bz2-ng's c/third_party/libsais/patches applied.
+ *
+ * 0001-keep-lms-positions.patch
+ */
+
 /*--
 
 This file is a part of libsais, a library for linear time suffix array,
@@ -6896,6 +6903,17 @@
         sa_sint_t first_lms_suffix    = SA[n - m];
         sa_sint_t left_suffixes_count = libsais_initialize_buckets_for_lms_suffixes_radix_sort_8u(T, buckets, first_lms_suffix);
 
+        /*
+         * Where the rest of the free space still lets the recursion sort
+         * without allocating, the LMS positions are kept in its last m ints
+         * for after the recursion instead of being found again by a second
+         * pass over T: fs >= m puts the copy beyond SA[0..n), and
+         * fs + n >= 4m leaves the recursion fs + n - 3m >= m ints of free
+         * space, at least its length.
+         */
+        sa_sint_t keep_lms_suffixes = fs >= m && (fs + n) / 4 >= m;
+        if (keep_lms_suffixes) { fs -= m; memcpy(&SA[n + fs], &SA[n - m], (size_t)m * sizeof(sa_sint_t)); }
+
         if (threads > 1 && n >= 65536) { memset(SA, 0, ((size_t)n - (size_t)m) * sizeof(sa_sint_t)); }
         libsais_radix_sort_lms_suffixes_8u_omp(T, SA, n, m, flags, buckets, threads, thread_state);
         if (threads > 1 && n >= 65536) { memset(&SA[(fast_sint_t)n - (fast_sint_t)m], 0, (size_t)m * sizeof(sa_sint_t)); }
@@ -6911,8 +6929,15 @@
                 return -2;
             }
 
-            libsais_gather_lms_suffixes_8u_omp(T, SA, n, threads, thread_state);
-            libsais_reconstruct_lms_suffixes_omp(SA, n, m, threads);
+            if (keep_lms_suffixes)
+            {
+                libsais_reconstruct_lms_suffixes_omp(SA, n + fs + m, m, threads);
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                libsais_gather_lms_suffixes_8u_omp(T, SA, n, threads, thread_state);
+                libsais_reconstruct_lms_suffixes_omp(SA, n, m, threads);
+            }
         }
 
         libsais_place_lms_suffixes_interval_8u(SA, n, m, flags, buckets);
